# SASL Web Application

Web-based version of the SASL Hand Detection System with real-time gesture recognition.

## Setup

1. Install dependencies:
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

2. Run the application:
```bash
python app.py
```

3. Open your browser and go to: http://localhost:5000

## Features

- Real-time SASL gesture recognition
- Hand detection with MediaPipe
- Web-based interface (no desktop app needed)
- Live video streaming
- Interactive controls
- 41 SASL gesture classes
- Hand-focused CNN-LSTM model with attention

## Usage

1. Click "Start Camera" to begin
2. Make SASL gestures in front of the camera
3. View predictions and confidence scores in real-time
4. Toggle hand detection overlay as needed
5. Reset buffer to clear prediction history

## Files

- `app.py` - Main Flask web application
- `models/class_names.json` - SASL gesture class names
- `models/hand_focused_sasl_model.pth` - Trained model weights
- `templates/index.html` - Web interface
- `requirements.txt` - Python dependencies